@H 1004_bigphi_faithful_clean := "With n AND discretization HELD IDENTICAL, do faithful_phi (MIP-EI scalar) and big-Φ (system Φ_s structure) actually disagree on the imagination/planning Φ-rise, or was H_1002's disagreement purely the n/discretization confound?" :: universe [GENUINE-MEASURE-DISAGREEMENT 🔴]
  seed     = "H_1002 found big-Φ DISAGREED with faithful_phi on the imagination/planning Φ-rise — but CONFOUNDED: big-Φ ran at n=4/binary-TPM while H_999/H_1001 faithful_phi ran at n=8/continuous-MI. H_1002 honestly marked itself ⚠ MEASURE-DEPENDENT and named the clean rung verbatim: same n, same discretization, both measures. This H runs that clean separation — collapse the two discretizations to ONE (the H_1002 binary path at n=4) and feed it to BOTH engines."
  target   = "🔴 GENUINE-MEASURE-DISAGREEMENT — at IDENTICAL (n=4, SAME binary discretization, both mirrors PROVEN ≡ stdlib at n=4), the planning Φ-rise disagreement SURVIVES matching (it is NOT the confound), while imagination+guided resolve to AGREE. H_971 imagination(DRIFT)−REACT: both RAISE (big-Φ +0.42 d+0.17 p0.51; faithful +0.06 d+0.13 p0.61) AGREE — faithful's n=8 d+2.09 shrinks to a matched-n=4 small null, so H_1002's imagination effect-collapse WAS the confound. H_988 guided−REACT: both RAISE (big-Φ +0.38 d+0.17; faithful +0.49 d+0.84 p2.0e-03) AGREE — faithful FLIPS from H_1002's −0.18 to +0.49, so H_1002's guided sign-mismatch WAS the confound. H_973 planning(d8)−GREEDY: big-Φ −4.01 (d−1.83, p2.5e-08, LOWERS) vs faithful +2.33 (d+5.18, p6.7e-27, RAISES) — a SIGN REVERSAL that PERSISTS at matched inputs, dose-response opposite (big-Φ rho+0.12 vs faithful rho−0.16). ⇒ for planning the MIP-EI scalar (cross-cut MI binds the branching trace UP) and the structure-level big-Φ (the binarized branching TPM is severed by the system MIP cheaply, DOWN) genuinely measure DIFFERENT things — a real, publishable IIT-internal finding BOUNDING H_999/H_1001's planning result to the MIP-EI measure. H_1002's confound explains imagination+guided but NOT planning."
  probe    = "UNIVERSE/h1004_bigphi_faithful_clean.py — ONE matched discretization (H_1002 binary path VERBATIM: top-4 variance channels binarized at own median → one n=4 binary state sequence) feeds BOTH engines: big-Φ ← empirical Laplace state-by-node TPM + modal sys_state (full IIT 4.0 system Φ_s mirror, distinctions+relations over the MIP); faithful_phi ← MI matrix over the SAME 4 binary unit-traces (n_bins=2, MIP-EI scalar min-cut MI / small-side). SAME n=4, SAME discretization — both H_1002 confounds (n shrink + binarization) REMOVED. 30 seeds, reuses the H_999/H_1002 regime harness VERBATIM. Both mirrors PROVEN ≡ their stdlib engines at n=4 (big-Φ ≡ iit4_bigphi.hexa on n=4 ring4 refs |Δ|<1e-6; faithful_phi ≡ faithful_phi.hexa on n=4 refs |Δ|<1e-4) + matched-path check (faithful-units==bits.T, no continuous leak)."
  verdict  = ".verdicts/1004_bigphi_faithful_clean/h1004_bigphi_faithful_clean.txt"
  scope    = "TOY single matched-rung n=4 (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck) — n=4 is the BINDING constraint (big-Φ super-exponential; at most n=5/6), chosen to match H_1002's big-Φ rung EXACTLY; both measures EXACT at n=4. WM latent binarized to an n=4 state-by-node TPM / n=4 binary units. The (n, discretization) is IDENTICAL across the two engines, so any remaining disagreement is GENUINELY measure-level, not the H_1002 confound — the entire purpose of this rung. Scale-transfer UNVERIFIED. g5 CODE-measured, no LLM self-judge (p7). NOT a forge binary; $0 CPU-local. xlink H_1002/H_999/H_1001, iit4_bigphi.hexa, iit4/faithful_phi.hexa, a_phi_iit4_tool, a_paper_negative_ok."
